# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this everything in the working
# directory is shipped into the build context and baked into a layer — including
# a Windows-built node_modules that the alpine image cannot use anyway, the whole
# git history, and the local mkcert keys.
#
# The .env files matter most: VITE_ variables are inlined into the bundle at
# build time, so a stray .env in the context can put a value into JavaScript that
# ships to every visitor.

node_modules
build
dist
coverage

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Local TLS for the https dev server. Never needed in an image, and a private key
# in a layer is a private key in a registry.
*.pem
*.key

# Real values arrive as build args (VITE_API_BASE_URL) and at runtime, never from
# a file in the context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.vscode
.idea
.claude
docs

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
